==Icelandic==
===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|is}} ''[[#Old Norse|kenna]]''.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈcʰɛnːa/|lang=is}}

===Verb===
{{is-verb-weak|kenndi|kennt}}

# to [[teach]], to [[tutor]]
#* Timothy 2:11-12 ([http://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=1+Timothy+2:11-12&version=NIV English], [http://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=1%20Timothy%202:11-12&version=ICELAND Icelandic])
#*: ''Konan á að læra í kyrrþey, í allri undirgefni. Ekki leyfi ég konu að '''kenna''' eða taka sér vald yfir manninum, heldur á hún að vera kyrrlát.''
#*:: A woman should learn in quietness and full submission. I do not permit a woman to '''teach''' or to have authority over a man; she must be silent.
# to [[instruct]]
# {{context|dated|lang=is}} to [[ascribe]]
